go`, I narrowed the socket-mode check (`checkCustodySocket`) from `perm&0o077` to `perm&0o070`. That admits sockets whose only extra permission bits are for \"other\", like 0602 or 0606. The full tmuxserver and termbind suites stayed green, in two separate runs.\n- **Why nothing caught it:** the only socket modes the tests use are 0600 (allowed) and 0644 (refused). 0644 has a group bit, so nothing ever checks the \"other\" bits on their own.\n- **Effect:** a socket anyone can connect to would pass custody at all three entry points (`Probe`, `Spawn` and `Execute`), while SPEC §3.2 requires an owner-only socket. The producer's own permission mutant only lets 0644 through, so it can't catch this.\n\n**Rework scope for the producer:**\n1. Add test rows for socket modes 0602, 0604, 0606 and 0620, driven through all three entry points. Each should assert the refusal (`tmux_unsafe_socket_path`, \"socket permissions\") and that no connect, spawn or dispatch happens.\n2. Ship my narrowing and its twin (`perm&0o007`) as harness mutants, each killed by a test run on its own.\n3. Update TRACEABILITY and the socket-permissions cell of the conformance matrix to list the mode cases.\n\n**What held up, all rerun by me on the exact candidate tree:**\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `go test ./... -count=1` | 45 of 45 packages pass |\n| `go vet`, native and Windows | clean |\n| gofmt | clean |\n| Registry digest and tracecheck | digest matches the pin; tracecheck output matches the README |\n| README coverage plant (81/585 changed to 82/585) | killed by `TestREADMEMeasuredCoverageMatchesTracecheckReport` |\n| Registry, decoded | every case from all four leaves is in its clause list; cpkajd's case is still in clause `2.4#2` |\n| Files trunk changed that the Story doesn't touch | all 63 identical to the base (the brief said 29) |\n| `task-board.config.json` | identical to the base |\n| Signatures on the three checkpoint commits | all verify |\n| Determinism, 8 new tests at `-count=3